WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.000
-How you doing? How's the fam?

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.167
How's the kids?
How's Faith Hill?

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:05.000
-I mean, everybody's great,
you know?

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.367
We got a 25-year-old,
a 23-year-old,

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:09.968
and a 20-year-old, all girls.

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.868
-I heard this now --
you guys are empty nesters now,

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:13.267
you and Faith.

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:15.734
-The best thing about it is,
you know, Faith said

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:18.133
the other night -- we were --
we had the fireplace going,

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:21.067
we had the doors open,
we were having a glass of wine.

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:26.000
And it was like -- Faith said,
"You know, it's like

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.801
we're the kids
and the parents are gone."

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:29.901
[ Laughter ]
-It's the opposite now.

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:31.200
You guys are having dance
parties and stuff? That's fun.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.567
-Oh, we're having dance parties.
We're having so much fun.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.400
I kind of like it.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.033
Then they come home
and they stay for like

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:42.100
three or four days,
and then it turns into a week.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.934
And then you're like,
"Mm, yeah."

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:46.267
-"We did this, now.
Yeah, come on! We did this!"

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.634
-"It's time to go."
-"We got a new life now, yeah."

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:49.834
You guys -- is this true? --

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:52.067
you celebrated 25 years
together, you and Faith?

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:55.601
-Yeah, 26 coming up in October.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:57.834
-You got to tell her --

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.901
You have to tell her hello
for me, please.

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:02.434
-I will.
-How did you propose to Faith?

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:04.234
Do you remember that?
-Yeah, I do.

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:07.701
We were pla--
I want to say it was Montana.

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:09.133
It was somewhere in
the middle of nowhere.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.934
We had this big festival,

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:14.200
and we had been touring together
for a little while.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.968
And it -- [ Chuckles ]

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:20.434
Apropos for a country music
concert,

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:24.400
we had trailer houses --
were our dressing rooms.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:25.801
-Sure.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:25.801 --> 00:01:27.834
We were doing this big festival,

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:29.901
and we were in
this trailer house.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:35.367
And I had, like,
my mirror and my --

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:37.968
my road case and everything
set up.

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:40.534
And I asked Faith, I said,
"Look."

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:42.234
This was right before
I went on stage.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.801
I said, "You know, I want you
to be my wife."

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:47.434
She goes, "Well, you've asked me
that several times."

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:48.834
I go, "This time I'm serious."

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:50.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.701
-Yeah, but this is --
you're in a trailer.

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:52.868
-Yeah, we're in a trailer.
-Yeah.

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.767
-She goes, "You're asking me
to marry you

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:57.400
at a country music festival
in a trailer park."

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.534
And I said, "Yes, ma'am, I am."

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:00.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:02.934
"You're from Mississippi.
I'm from Louisiana.

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:04.968
It seems pretty appropriate."
-Yeah.

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:07.601
-And then when I came back
offstage,

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:10.934
she had written in lipstick,
"Yes, I'm gonna be your wife."

00:02:10.934 --> 00:02:12.701
[ Audience awws ]
[ Applause ]

00:02:12.701 --> 00:02:14.534
Yeah.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.868
-That's fantastic.
-And I still have that mirror.

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:18.434
-You have the mirror?
-I still have the mirror.

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:20.100
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.801
Tim, I've known you
for a while now.

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:24.200
I got to tell you -- you are
unbelievable in "1883."

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.300
-Ah, thank you.
-You hit it out
of the park, man.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.000
This is unbelievable.
-Yes.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.767
-I mean, wow!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:32.200
You crushed it, buddy.
You crushed it.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.100
And you're also
back on the road.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.400
-Yeah, we're touring right now.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.467
Tomorrow night I'm in Cleveland.
-Wow.

00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:39.467
How's it feel to be back on --
-"Hello, Cleveland."

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:40.968
-"Hello, Cleveland.

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:43.868
You made four rights, well,
that's a circle," yeah.

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:47.100
How is it performing in front of
live audiences again?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.367
-It's so awesome.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:51.200
It's been six years since
I've done a solo tour.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.400
-Geez.
-Yeah, the last tour was

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.968
Faith and I doing "Soul2Soul,"
which was '17-'18.

00:02:56.968 --> 00:03:00.901
But I'm glad to be back with
my band, my guys, you know,

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:02.868
and playing music
and playing new songs.

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:04.033
And we're in the middle of

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:05.667
recording a new album
at the same time.

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:06.901
-That's what I'm talking about.
-Yeah.

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:08.334
-That's part of you.
That's part of your brain.

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:10.767
That's the way you work.
-I like to work, you know.

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:12.267
-You're Tim McGraw, yeah.

00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:16.534
And what's it like working with
Faith as your wife on "1883"?

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:18.200
-It was good.
-Yeah.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.901
You definitely, I mean --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.367
-It was good.
-Yeah.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:25.067
-And we said, "You know, it's
gonna be tough because people

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:27.000
are going to see Faith and Tim
on screen,

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.734
and we have to overcome that."
-Yeah.

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:30.801
-And so we sort of gave
each other a high-five

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:32.901
and gave each other a kiss
and said, "You know what?

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:35.334
The only way to do it is
just try to be good at it."

00:03:35.334 --> 00:03:38.701
-Yeah, and boy --
-However...

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:43.968
However, there was a scene that
we did where she had to slap me.

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:45.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:47.033
-But it's not a real slap.
It's a TV slap.

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:48.534
-No, that was a real slap.

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:50.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:52.167
No.
-Was that your idea?

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:54.334
-Well, we talked about it
before.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.434
You know, we don't want to do
a TV slap.

00:03:56.434 --> 00:03:59.133
We want to do a real slap, but
after about the eighth take...

00:03:59.133 --> 00:04:02.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.567
-Faith is like, "I need one
more. I need one more.

00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:05.334
Let's do one more.
I need one for me."

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.968
-I was concussed a bit.

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:11.334
And I told her afterward,
I said, "Do we need to talk?"

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:13.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.534
"Is there something going on
I don't know about?"

00:04:14.534 --> 00:04:15.934
-That's so funny. Oh, my God.

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:18.234
-'Cause, you know, I was
expecting like, a good...

00:04:18.234 --> 00:04:19.701
You know, finger slap.
-Yeah.

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:21.467
-No, it was a palm.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:23.000
-She's, like, closing her fist.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.167
You're like
"Hey, don't punch me," yeah.

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:27.067
-It was like Rocky hitting me.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:30.234
-Can we explain to everyone
what "1883" is about?

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:34.834
-Well, "1883" is sort of the
origin story of "Yellowstone,"

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:36.868
which I know a lot of you guys
have seen "Yellowstone."

00:04:36.868 --> 00:04:38.133
-Yeah. Absolutely.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:38.133 --> 00:04:40.601
-Yeah.

00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:42.834
Which I'm a huge fan of.

00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:44.901
Faith and I have both been
a huge fan of since

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:47.033
the very first night
of the very first show.

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:49.601
And then, Taylor Sheridan
called,

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:52.300
who's one of
the most brilliant writers

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.167
in the history of Hollywood.
-Right?

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:56.667
-The way he writes.
And he asked if I would do

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:59.567
some flashback stuff
for "Yellowstone."

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:03.667
And then, long story short,
you know, I wanted to do it.

00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:06.734
I said, "But I don't want to be
this country singer

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:08.901
that shows up at the bunkhouse

00:05:08.901 --> 00:05:10.400
and gets taken to
the train station.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.901
So, if we can come up with
something cool..."

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:15.901
And he came up with the idea of
us being the original Duttons

00:05:15.901 --> 00:05:18.267
who founded
the Yellowstone dynasty.

00:05:18.267 --> 00:05:21.033
-And what a layered character
you play.

00:05:21.033 --> 00:05:22.868
-Yeah, it was so cool.

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:24.968
You know, and Faith and I have
never acted together.

00:05:24.968 --> 00:05:27.534
You know, we'd never done
anything on screen together,

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:29.434
other than videos, and it was --

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:31.834
-Yeah, just toured together.
-Yeah, just toured together.

00:05:31.834 --> 00:05:33.000
So it was so cool to be able
to work with her.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.334
-She's great as well.
-Yeah.

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:37.534
She blew me away
every single day.

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:40.100
You know, she was so nervous.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:42.234
She had done two movies before.

00:05:42.234 --> 00:05:44.534
And I'd done a few movie--
handful of movies.

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:47.734
But she showed up every day
and just blew me away.

00:05:47.734 --> 00:05:50.133
-Yeah.
-She elevated my game every day.

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:52.734
-You two together, man. Yeah,
you were fantastic as well.

00:05:52.734 --> 00:05:54.000
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.000
Here's Tim McGraw in "1883."
Take a look at this.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.033
-You got it all figured out,
don't you?

00:06:11.234 --> 00:06:13.367
You say you love her.

00:06:13.367 --> 00:06:15.767
But you won't ever love her
like I do.

00:06:17.534 --> 00:06:19.667
That's my heart
you're running off with.

00:06:21.267 --> 00:06:23.400
You better cradle it
like an egg.

00:06:24.367 --> 00:06:26.367
-That's what I'm talking about!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:26.367 --> 00:06:29.767
You crushed it, buddy!
You crushed it!

00:06:29.767 --> 00:06:31.834
I'm sure I'll be seeing you
at these award shows.

00:06:31.834 --> 00:06:33.234
Tim McGraw, everybody.

00:06:33.234 --> 00:06:36.767
"1883" is streaming now
on Paramount+.

00:06:36.767 --> 00:06:41.133
Go check it out, and go see him
on tour, his "McGraw Tour 2022."

